Lab 1: Readiness Failure & Traffic Isolation
Goal: Verify that a failing readiness probe stops traffic routing without killing the container.

Observation: When /healthz was missing, the deployment reported 0/1 READY, and kubectl get endpoints probe-service returned <none>.

Resolution: Creating the /healthz file inside the pod instantly allowed the readiness probe to pass, adding the Pod's IP back into the EndpointSlice.


Lab 2: Dynamic Volume Provisioning & Persistence
Goal: Verify data durability across pod deletion.

Implementation:

Requested storage using a PersistentVolumeClaim named web-data-pvc (500Mi, ReadWriteOnce).

The default StorageClass automatically provisioned a PersistentVolume and transitioned the claim to Bound.

Wrote data inside the mounted directory:

kubectl exec $POD_NAME -- sh -c 'echo "Kubernetes Day 2 Storage Confirmed" > /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html'

Deleted the pod with kubectl delete pod $POD_NAME.

The Deployment controller spawned a replacement pod, re-mounted the exact same PV, and confirmed data persistence when querying /usr/share/nginx/html/index.html.

